# A guest throws a rock into the wall, then one into a standing dummy. Its own throws fly with no
# delay (the seam never moves a body the guest simulates), and the dummy falls for everyone by the
# guest's impact claim, once.
scenario throw_dummy
scene dummy_wall
seed 23
guests 1
settle 8s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 20ms loss 2%

p1 grab rock_a as lift_a
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw wall speed 9 as wall
p1 wait 1s
p1 walk rock_b
p1 grab rock_b as lift_b
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw dummy speed 9 as dummy

expect result lift_a granted
expect result lift_b granted
expect result wall done
expect result dummy done
expect effect dummy
expect effects_once
# The dummy fell by the guest's claim, and an honest guest sends nothing the parser refuses.
expect claims.count >= 1
expect claim_effects.count >= 1
expect claims_format.count <= 0
# Derived as in layer_bounce: a body this guest simulates is moved by the seam only when it becomes
# local, and the render offset takes that move: float noise, 1 cm.
expect local_correction.max <= 1cm
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
